from __future__ import annotations

__doc__ = """
OpenCL backend generation and kernel-oriented source emission.

This backend lowers Phoenix routines to OpenCL C kernels and helper routines,
mapping multiframe expansion onto work-item and work-group identifiers where
appropriate. It complements the OpenCL ADAA and wrapper layers that manage
device-resident data and runtime program compilation.
"""

__doc__ = """
OpenCL code-generation backend.

The OpenCL backend follows the same lowering strategy as the C backend for
affine and bilinear updates, but emits OpenCL C source instead of host C code.
Routines that consume multiframe selectors through an
:class:`OpenCLDeviceResource` become kernels and map those selectors to
``get_local_id`` / ``get_group_id`` requests. Routines without kernel requests
remain plain device helper functions.
"""

